<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>ErdasIMG: Conversion between LAN or GIS (Erdas) files and IMG</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
	This program allows putting several IMG files into one
  Erdas file of type LAN or GIS. On the other hand, it can also extract all
  the image bands contained on a LAN file and save them into different IMG
  files. GIS files only have one band and they are usually thematic files, not
  radiometric images.

  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 
  <p>In the conversion from GIS to IMG, if a TRL file, containing the color
  palette and the class names, exists, a file P25 with the palette will be
  created; class names are stored in the DOC file.</p>

  <p>In the conversion from IMG to GIS, DOC file categories are written into
  the TRL file, as well as palette colors, that are extracted from the P25
  file given at the command line.</p>

  <p>This program runs with Erdas files version 7.4 .</p>

  <p>The Erdas format is appropriate to work with Erdas, Arc/Info and
  ArcView.</p>
  <hr/>
  Erdas, Arc/Info and ArcView are registered trademarks of their respective
  owners.<br/>
